course: dictionary
lesson: 6975
title: Spotting panicky words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Panicky is an informal word. It describes feeling or showing sudden, great fear or worry, so that you cannot think calmly. You will hear it in stories and in everyday talk.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Scammers do not usually guess; they trick» tells you that the next part is a trap. A panicky message tries to make you feel scared, so you act fast without thinking. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put panicky in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: When you feel panicky yourself, the safe thing is to stop, breathe and think. Then find a safe adult to check with. Never type your login into a link just because a message is urgent.
fact: Panicky means feeling or showing sudden great fear or worry, so that you cannot think calmly.
fact: Panicky is an informal word, so you will meet it more in chat and everyday talk than in formal writing.
fact: You can talk about «a panicky voice» or «a panicky crowd» to show fear spreading quickly.
fact: Scam messages often sound panicky, such as «Your account will be deleted, log in here now!», to push you to act without thinking.
fact: If you feel panicky, stop, breathe and find a safe adult before you do anything else.
exercise: «Your account will be deleted, log in here now!» is a panicky message. What does panicky mean? | Feeling calm and relaxed about a message | *Feeling sudden great fear or worry, so you cannot think calmly | Feeling very happy and excited | Feeling bored and tired
exercise: Which word in «log in here now» tells you to act quickly? | log | in | *now | here
exercise: Mia feels panicky after she loses Mum in the shop. What is the best first step? | Run out of the shop alone | Keep walking fast in any direction | Ignore it and keep shopping | *Stop, breathe and find a safe adult
test: The crowd was panicky after the alarm rang. What does panicky describe? | Hungry and tired | Feeling calm and sleepy | *Sudden great fear, so that people cannot think calmly | Happy and singing
test: Why do scammers use panicky messages? | To help you find a lost pet | To make you sure they are your friend | *To rush you into acting before you think | To give you free prizes for no reason
exam: Which option best describes panicky? | *Sudden great fear or worry, so you cannot think calmly | Calm and thoughtful | Full of light and glowing | Quiet and gloomy
